oc get pods -n health-probe-lab
You should see 2/2 containers running (application + Istio proxy).

Check the sidecar configuration:
oc describe pod -l app=health-demo -n health-probe-lab
Subtask 2.3: Create Istio Virtual Service and Destination Rule
Create a Virtual Service to manage traffic routing. Save as virtual-service.yaml:
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: health-demo-vs
  namespace: health-probe-lab
spec:
  hosts:
  - health-demo-service
  http:
  - match:
    - headers:
        end-user:
          exact: test
    route:
    - destination:
        host: health-demo-service
        subset: v1
      weight: 100
  - route:
    - destination:
        host: health-demo-service
        subset: v1
      weight: 100
---
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: DestinationRule
metadata:
  name: health-demo-dr
  namespace: health-probe-lab
spec:
  host: health-demo-service
  subsets:
  - name: v1
    labels:
      version: v1
  trafficPolicy:
    outlierDetection:
      consecutiveErrors: 3
      interval: 30s
      baseEjectionTime: 30s
      maxEjectionPercent: 50
    healthCheck:
      path: /health/ready
      intervalSeconds: 10
      timeoutSeconds: 3
      unhealthyThreshold: 3
      healthyThreshold: 2
Apply the Istio configuration:
oc apply -f virtual-service.yaml
Verify the configuration:
oc get virtualservice,destinationrule -n health-probe-lab
